Create a high-level, repository-level component diagram showing only the application's main runtime components and how they directly interact. For a service-backed application, show components such as the UI, service/API, and database, with arrows showing that the UI calls the service and the service reads from or writes to the database when supported by the input. Treat this as a simple view of the application's runtime structure, not a domain model or a file/folder map. Exclude configuration files, settings, environment variables, framework wiring, libraries, build/deployment details, and any item that only configures or supports another component. Do not infer components or connections not supported by the input; keep the diagram to the few components a reader needs to understand the application. {{FLOWCHART_SYNTAX_NOTE}}
Every flowchart node must be clickable: after the edge definitions, add one 'click <node id> "<note path>"' statement per node, using the exact note path for the source repository from the link targets listed above (e.g. 'click booking "repo-a/README.md"'). Multiple nodes may link to the same repository note.